    {% filter nhsukMarkdown %}
Use this guide to create a spreadsheet of pupil data for the vaccination team.

This guide is for school office staff and MIS managers who use SIMS.

> You need permission to design and run reports in SIMS. If you do not have it, ask your MIS manager.

## Export pupil data

Check you are logged in to the SIMS instance for the school you’re providing information for.

1. Go to **Reports**, then **Design Report**.
2. Select **Create a new report**, then choose **Student** as the data area.
3. Select the data fields you need, then select **Next**.
4. Filter by the school you’re providing information for.
5. Filter by the year groups you’re providing information for.
6. Set the report destination to **Export as CSV**.
7. Save the report, then select **Run**.

## Select the school

SIMS holds data for one school, so there is no school filter.

Check you are logged in to the SIMS instance for the school you’re providing information for. If your trust uses a shared SIMS environment, use the school selector when you log in.

## Select the year groups

1. On the filter step, select **Year Group** from the field list.
2. Select the year groups you’re providing information for.
3. Add a second filter for **Student Status** and set it to **On Roll**, then select **Next**.

